  "findings": [
    {
      "area": "MCP boundary",
      "result": "Production dependencies are protocol/service plus transport/runtime libraries. Store is dev-only. Handler dispatches through Service; current authority is checked before tool projection/execution. No direct SQLite access in reviewed adapter production code."
    },
    {
      "area": "Example state ownership",
      "result": "Example production depends on the public client, not Connect store/service/server. Its SQLite is separately bound application state with process locks, schema checks and immutable binding verification. Read-only inspection does not claim or edit Connect server state."
    },
    {
      "area": "Cancellation and bounds",
      "result": "MCP handler distinguishes cancelled/expired work as transport-uncertain, retains correlation IDs and directs reconciliation. The shared capacity pool limits listeners and requests to 32 with immediate overload; bounded wait reserves time for current authority and response projection. Shutdown observation distinguishes expected stop from unexpected exit."
    },
    {
      "area": "Module structure",
      "result": "Task runners, application journal/state, MCP and provider bootstrap responsibilities use separate modules. Larger existing top-level protocol/client files remain; no arbitrary line-count threshold is claimed. Main delegates Gate 4 task access, diagnostics and Vapi host work to CLI modules rather than implementing those workflows inline."
    }
  ],
